{
  "notes": "Transfer completion and recovery, the shared seam every client derives per refresh (docs/contracts/ui.md Smart home, client-storage.md Focused journey, native-data.md). All arithmetic is in printed clock minutes: floor every instant to its minute before subtracting, so a window agrees with the two clock times printed beside it. The window of the change after leg i is w = floor(dep(i+1)) - floor(arr(i)) over effective times: w >= 5 ordinary, 0 < w < 5 or shrunk below the printed window tight, w <= 0 lost, a cancelled leg either side broken and never tight or lost. A recovery candidate must clear the same floor the server uses for a connection, w >= 3 against arr(i). Times are epoch milliseconds; clock strings are Australia/Sydney. Each case starts from base.legs, then applies legs (full replacement), estimates (per-leg effective override) and cancelledLegs. searches are the recovery searches available to the case, keyed by id, with the anchor the client must use (from, at); expected.search names the one search a refresh is allowed to make and expected.candidate indexes its journeys. heldRecovery is the record already on disk, previous the prior observation an alert cue compares against. followedChanges are the states of the followed journey's changes and composedChanges those of the composed journey that is rendered; recoveryAnchor is a composed-journey change index. Instruction and receipt strings are the model's text before the warn idiom's capitalisation; status and changeLabels are as printed.",
